                <li>Back Bay Station is convenient for travelers in that neighborhood, but it has fewer train departures.</li>
                <li>Route 128 Station is useful for suburban travelers but offers limited facilities and fewer departure options.</li>
                <li>Massachusetts Context: South Station serves as the primary hub for trains heading southwest to Bridgeport, while Back Bay provides a secondary option for travelers in the western part of downtown Boston.</li>
